# first parent ac60733caed8178411071c5b4ed88994a657ea7f
# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: exact start-from resolution, --start-from-file/--opaque-file, CHARON_CALLGRAPH
#
# Start-from patterns that the rustc path resolver cannot resolve (disambiguators, impl blocks inside
# a path, closures, promoted constants, closure impls and methods, defaulted methods, drop glue
# impls, vtables) are resolved exactly as Charon names: `resolve_exact` indexes the definitions of
# a crate by the parent they are named under and compares impl blocks with rustc's self and trait
# types, without registering items. A selection of a function, type, trait or impl now covers that
# item only (modules and inherent impls still cover their contents); `start_from_selected` in the
# coverage report lists the selected items at translation time. An unmatched strict pattern is an
# error naming it.
#
# `--start-from-file`/`--opaque-file` (charon binary) append one pattern per line to
# `--start-from`/`--opaque`, leaving the serialized options unchanged.
#
# `CHARON_CALLGRAPH=<file>` writes, after translation and before the passes, every translated item
# with its canonical pattern (checked to parse back and to match the item; other items it matches are
# listed), kind, crate, module, generics, body size and dependency edges (signature and body, as the
# declaration graph records them); global initializers, promoted constants and constructors are
# folded into their owner. `CHARON_CALLGRAPH_ONLY=1` stops there. Format documented in callgraph.rs.
# The name matcher no longer asserts when an impl's trait is a partial monomorphization instance.

